    "note_tweet": {
      "entities": {},
      "text": "It seems neither shadcn nor its users ever need to pick a year, as if AI-generated projects are so short-lived that nobody needs to select a date from more than a year ago.\nWith shadcn, after manually entering a date, you can at least open the native date picker. It may not be beautifully designed, but it gets the job done. Yours, on the other hand, requires clicking the \"previous month\" button 12 times just to go back one year. What if the user is selecting their birthday?"
